// Title: Potential Suspicious Windows Feature Enabled
// ID: 55c925c1-7195-426b-a136-a9396800e29b
// Status: test
// Level: medium
// Author: frack113
// Date: 2022-09-10
// Tags: attack.stealth
// Description: Detects usage of the built-in PowerShell cmdlet "Enable-WindowsOptionalFeature" used as a Deployment Image Servicing and Management tool.
// Similar to DISM.exe, this cmdlet is used to enumerate, install, uninstall, configure, and update features and packages in Windows images
// Converted by: Sigma Universal SIEM/EDR CLI

(((where(ScriptBlockText ICONTAINS "Enable-WindowsOptionalFeature") AND where(ScriptBlockText ICONTAINS "-Online") AND where(ScriptBlockText ICONTAINS "-FeatureName"))) AND ((where(ScriptBlockText ICONTAINS "TelnetServer") OR where(ScriptBlockText ICONTAINS "Internet-Explorer-Optional-amd64") OR where(ScriptBlockText ICONTAINS "TFTP") OR where(ScriptBlockText ICONTAINS "SMB1Protocol") OR where(ScriptBlockText ICONTAINS "Client-ProjFS") OR where(ScriptBlockText ICONTAINS "Microsoft-Windows-Subsystem-Linux"))))
